          "inheritance": "not reported",
          "parental_testing_statement": "The homozygous state for the missense mutation was confirmed by sequencing genomic DNA from his parents, who were T/C heterozygotes at position c.667. In addition, both parents turned out to be G/A heterozygotes for SNP rs2744583, providing further evidence that they carried two copies of the SSADH gene not deleted in exon 4.",
          "functional_evidence_statement": "not reported",
          "pathogenicity_as_stated_by_authors": "novel missense mutation; 'strongly supporting the pathogenic role of this novel nucleotide alteration' (same amino acid as c.668G>A, reported with dramatic reduction of enzyme activity, Akaboshi et al. 2003)",
